  message: "[REVIEW 2026-11-15: REAL TODAY, TEXT PARTLY STALE] 2026-11-15, dev e2b6ab8096. Behaviour unchanged: stable_id and shape_id emit `sha256:<16hex>`, repo_fingerprint `sha256:<64hex>` (so does analysis_runs[].pass_version), fingerprint `hgfp2:`. No `hgstableid`/`hgshapeid`/`hgrepofp` prefix and no digest-compatibility field in packages/*/src, the spec or the changelog. stable_id scheme is v14 (WI-ruful, 2026-11-12), so the relabel number in the 11-01 header is taken; v10-v14 are all unreleased (tag v9.2.0 carries v9). Constants: schema.py:149/161/168/173; validator pattern spec_validator.py:1951. 75 test files match the `sha256:` prefix. ir.py:606-616 still carries WI-tisar's 2026-07-15 text that stable_id/shape_id need no in-value discriminator. Full review: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/reports/WI-talos.md. No status or priority change made by this review."  # a347
- op: discuss  # dc3c
  at: '2026-11-15T19:47:30Z'  # dc3c
  by: agent  # dc3c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dc3c
  clock: 12  # dc3c
  nonce: dc3c  # dc3c
  message: "[INVESTIGATION 2026-11-15, owner-requested: which ruling stands, this item's or WI-tisar's; dev e2b6ab8096] THE RECORD. WI-tisar-fomul-satoz-pufoj-pupam-vijup-bival-tosuj (done) carries an owner-ratified DOCUMENT verdict of 2026-07-15: do not prefix stable_id or shape_id; `sha256:` names the algorithm; the field name and the top-level *_scheme descriptors discriminate; a relabel would churn every serialized value. It shipped as text (37e0252d5b): ir.py:606-616 and two passages of docs/schema.json. This item carries an OWNER DECISION of 2026-07-29, two weeks later: every identity value gets its own versioned prefix (hgstableid<N>:, hgshapeid<N>:, hgrepofp<N>:), labels only, digests unchanged, with a digest-compatibility declaration. The 07-29 entry does not mention WI-tisar-fomul-satoz-pufoj-pupam-vijup-bival-tosuj, and WI-tisar-fomul-satoz-pufoj-pupam-vijup-bival-tosuj has no entry saying it was superseded. READING. The later decision is the more specific one, answers the earlier cost argument (digests unchanged, compatibility declared) and addresses a harm the earlier verdict did not weigh: repo_fingerprint also emits `sha256:`, so three of the four schemes are indistinguishable in a value. So this item's decision stands and the ir.py / schema.json text is correct only as a description of what ships today. What the record cannot show is that the 07-15 verdict was weighed on 07-29; that is the one thing for the owner to confirm. WHAT IN THE 07-29 SPEC IS OUT OF DATE EITHER WAY. (1) Numbers: v9 and v10 were used by other bumps (v9 WI-tusad 10-13, v10 WI-banod T1 10-22) and dev is at v14, so the relabel would be v15, with shapeid v4 and repofp v3. (2) The \"two releases\" gate: the last release, v9.2.0 (2026-10-20), carries stableid-v9 and v10-v14 are unreleased, so the next release already crosses five digest-changing bumps; a relabel in that same release costs a consumer no extra re-keying, and a digest-compatibility field would have nothing to promise. (3) Two producers under one field: the SCIP arm still hashes outside the factories (scip/index.py:282-290; 09-18 entries), so one prefix per field would label two algorithms alike. (4) Counts: 75 test files assert the `sha256:` prefix (63 when written); constants at schema.py:149/161/168/173; validator pattern at spec_validator.py:1951. Also sharing the prefix and absent from the spec: analysis_runs[].pass_version, config_fingerprint, run_signature. BEARING ON CURRENT WORK. A store that keeps stable ids across runs (the stored-graph plan, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_plan_11152026.md step 1d) must record stable_id_scheme beside them in either case; if the relabel is wanted, doing it before such a store exists avoids migrating it. RECOMMENDATION, owner's call, nothing changed: confirm this item's decision over WI-tisar-fomul-satoz-pufoj-pupam-vijup-bival-tosuj's; ship the relabel in the same release as v10-v14 and drop the compatibility field; decide the SCIP arm's label in the same change; move the decision into ADR-0035 when it ships, replace the ir.py and schema.json text in that PR, and add a superseded note on WI-tisar-fomul-satoz-pufoj-pupam-vijup-bival-tosuj."  # dc3c
