- op: update  # f1cb
  at: '2026-11-15T19:57:55Z'  # f1cb
  by: agent  # f1cb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f1cb
  clock: 14  # f1cb
  nonce: f1cb  # f1cb
  set:  # f1cb
    description: "[RE-BASED 2026-11-15 by owner ruling. dev e2b6ab8096]\nThe 2026-07-29 decision STANDS over WI-tisar-fomul-satoz-pufoj-pupam-vijup-bival-tosuj's 2026-07-15 \"document, do not prefix\" verdict: every identity value\ngets its own readable, hg-namespaced, versioned prefix; labels only, digests not recomputed; `fingerprint` (hgfp2:)\nis already in that form.\n\nThe spec, re-based on today's tree:\n  * NUMBERS. v9 and v10 were used by other bumps and dev is at stableid-v14 / shapeid-v3 / repofp-v2. The relabel\n    takes the next number of each scheme when it ships: hgstableid15:, hgshapeid4:, hgrepofp3: if nothing else\n    bumps first.\n  * WHEN. The last release, v9.2.0, carries stableid-v9 and v10-v14 are unreleased, so the next release already\n    crosses five digest-changing bumps. Ship the relabel in that same release. In that case the\n    digest-compatibility declaration of DECISION 2 has nothing to promise and is not built; if the relabel instead\n    ships after a release that already carries v14, DECISION 2 applies as written.\n  * TWO PRODUCERS. The rust-analyzer (SCIP) arm computes stable_id outside the factories (scip/index.py:282-290).\n    Decide its label in the same change: adopt the factories, or declare its own scheme and prefix. One prefix over\n    two algorithms is not acceptable (09-18 entries).\n  * WHERE IT IS WRITTEN DOWN. Move the decision into ADR-0035 in the PR that ships it, and in that PR replace the\n    text WI-tisar-fomul-satoz-pufoj-pupam-vijup-bival-tosuj shipped (ir.py:606-616 and the two passages of docs/schema.json), which is correct until then.\n  * SITES. Constants schema.py:149/161/168/173; validator pattern spec_validator.py:1951; 75 test files assert the\n    `sha256:` prefix. Not in the 07-29 spec and sharing the prefix: analysis_runs[].pass_version,\n    config_fingerprint, run_signature -- decide for each whether it is in scope and say so.\n\nA store that persists stable ids across runs must record stable_id_scheme beside them until this ships.\n\n--- text before the re-basing ---\n[REVIEW 2026-11-01, PARTLY-STALE] 2026-11-01 review @100b6fbb6e: the declarations now read stableid-v13 / shapeid-v3 / repofp-v2 / symbol-fp-v2. Emitted values: stable_id sha256:<16hex>, shape_id sha256:<16hex>, repo_fingerprint sha256:<64hex> (config_fingerprint and run_signature also sha256:); fingerprint hgfp2:. No hgstableid/hgshapeid/hgrepofp prefix exists in src. The collision complaint holds. Stale parts: the owner plan's 'v9 = relabel, v10 = bitbake' numbering was used up by WI-tusad (v9) and WI-banod (v10), so the relabel is now v14 and the prefixes need new numbers. The undeclared-SCIP-scheme concern from 2026-09-18 is now declared: v11 (INV-kutid) names scip_stable_id in the spec history. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)"  # f1cb
